// The GATT database this host exposes, which is only its own name.
//
// Two lines, and they are BTstack's example boilerplate with the name changed -
// the syntax is fixed by BTstack's GATT compiler. See README here for the
// BSD-3-Clause notice that covers it.
//
// Keep the name in step with gap_set_local_name() in bt_app.c: this is what a
// connected peer reads, that is what it sees while scanning, and two different
// answers to "what is this device called" is a confusing thing to debug.
PRIMARY_SERVICE, GAP_SERVICE
CHARACTERISTIC, GAP_DEVICE_NAME, READ, "piegpu"
